.TH OSINIT 8
.SH NAME
osinit \- first program of the native kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /osinit.dis
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Osinit
is the Limbo program the native (bare-metal) kernel starts when the Dis
virtual machine is up.
It is compiled into the kernel image, takes no arguments, and turns a
kernel with devices into a machine with a namespace, a network, a card
and a shell.
The hosted emulator does not use it; see
.IR init (8).
.PP
It does the following, in this order.
.IP 1.
Checks of the machine it has been given, each of which prints a line:
the kernel image read back from
.IR boot (3)
with its SHA-1, a GPIO pin driven and read, every core's clock ticking,
the command line, an integer benchmark and a run of the JIT across the
instruction set.
If the command line holds the word
.BR tryboot ,
it prints how to keep or reject this kernel.
.IP 2.
Binds the kernel's devices:
.B #I
before
.BR /net ,
.B #p
on
.BR /prog ,
.B #e
on
.BR /env ,
.B #u
on
.BR /usb ,
.B #s
on
.BR /chan ,
.B #A
after
.BR /dev .
(The kernel has already bound
.BR #c ", " #m ", " #S ", " #B ", " #G ", " #T
and
.BR #b .)
.IP 3.
Configures the loopback interface.
.IP 4.
Reads the master boot record from
.BR /dev/sdcard ,
names each partition to
.IR sd (3)
as
.BR sd0 ", " sd1 ...,
and runs
.IR dossrv (4)
on the first FAT partition, mounting it on
.BR /n/dos .
With no card this is silent.
.IP 5.
Applies
.BR /n/dos/rootpath :
see below.
.IP 6.
Gives the Wi-Fi driver the names of its firmware files in
.BR /n/dos/firmware .
.IP 7.
Mounts an 8MB memory file system on
.BR /tmp .
.IP 8.
If
.B /n/dos/wifi
exists, joins that network; if
.B /n/dos/bt
exists, starts
.IR bt9p (4)
and writes it that file's lines.
.IP 9.
Starts
.B touch.dis
for a touch panel; starts
.B "etherusb -k"
if
.B #l/ether0/addr
is already non-zero, that being a network device the kernel drives itself
(see
.IR ether (3)).
.IP 10.
In processes of their own, and not waited for: walks the USB bus,
starting
.BR kbdusb ,
.BR mouseusb ,
.B etherusb
and, on a machine with an xHCI controller,
.B diskusb
(a mass-storage device served as
.B /chan/usbdiskN
and mounted on
.BR /n/usbN ;
the console shell, whose namespace was forked before the driver ran,
mounts it itself with
.BR "dossrv -f /chan/usbdisk0 -m /n/usb0" )
for what it finds and watching hubs for changes; and, if
.B /n/dos/netconsole
exists, serves a shell on TCP port 17010.
.IP 11.
Writes
.B booted
to
.BR /dev/sysctl ,
releasing the boot watchdog, and runs
.B "sh -l"
on the console.
.PP
.B Sh -l
reads
.BR /lib/sh/profile ,
which in the kernel image is
.BR /os/init/profile :
it starts
.B auth/secstored
and, in the background,
.BR /lib/lucifer/boot-baremetal.sh .
That script forks its namespace; removes
.B #S
and
.B #G
from it and binds
.B /dev/null
over
.B /dev/sysctl
and
.BR /dev/hostowner ;
verifies that they are gone and stops if not; and then asks the draw
device whether there is a screen.
With none the machine is
.IR headless :
the script says so and starts nothing.
Otherwise it runs
.B wm/logon
(unless
.B /n/dos/skiplogon
exists) and the Lucifer desktop.
The console remains a shell with the whole namespace in either case.
.SS "Files on the card"
All are optional.
.TP
.B rootpath
Where user programs come from; one source a line, applied in order.
.B local
unions the card's
.BR dis ,
.BR lib ,
.B fonts
and
.B icons
after the kernel's own and binds its
.B usr
over
.B /usr
for writing.
.BI "net " addr
mounts the file server at dial string
.IR addr ,
unauthenticated, on
.B /n/remote
and does the same from there.
Without the file the policy is
.BR local .
.TP
.B wifi
Lines
.BI essid " name"
and
.BI password " phrase" \fR,\fP
the value being the rest of the line.
.TP
.B bt
Control lines for
.BR /net/bt ,
written in order; blank lines and lines beginning
.B #
are skipped.
.TP
.B btkeys
Where
.I bt9p
keeps link keys.
.TP
.B netconsole
Its existence enables the network console.
If it has a first line, that is a token a client must send, in clear,
before it is given a shell; if it is empty there is none, and
.I osinit
says so loudly.
.TP
.B skiplogon
Its existence starts the desktop without
.BR wm/logon ,
.I factotum
or
.IR secstore .
.SH FILES
.TF /lib/lucifer/boot-baremetal.sh
.TP
.B /osinit.dis
in the kernel's root
.TP
.B /n/dos
the card's FAT partition
.TP
.B /os/init/profile
.B /lib/sh/profile
in the kernel's root
.TP
.B /lib/lucifer/boot-baremetal.sh
narrows the namespace; starts the desktop if there is a screen
.SH SOURCE
.B /os/init/osinit.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR boot (3),
.IR cons (3),
.IR ether (3),
.IR sd (3),
.IR bt9p (4),
.IR dossrv (4),
.IR init (8),
.IR wpa (8)
.br
.B /docs/BAREMETAL.md
.SH BUGS
Every process it starts, the desktop's included, runs as the host owner.
.br
The network console's token and the
.B wifi
file's passphrase are clear text, the first on the network and the second
on a FAT card.
.br
The self-checks of step 1 run on every boot and take some seconds.
